BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Montclair State University
CATEGORIES:ThoughtfulLearning
CATEGORIES:Academic/Educational/Intellectual
CATEGORIES:Leadership
CATEGORIES:Service
DESCRIPTION:Honor the spirit of service on Montclair State University's An
 nual 9/11 Day of Service by helping ensure every eligible Red Hawk has th
 e opportunity to make their voice heard.\nJoin the Office of Civic and Vo
 ter Engagement for Race to the Ballot: Campus Takeover\, a campus-wide se
 rvice initiative that empowers students to become civic ambassadors. Duri
 ng this hands-on volunteer experience\, you'll learn how to confidently e
 ngage your peers in nonpartisan conversations about voting\, assist them 
 with the voter registration process\, and encourage them to make a pledge
  to show up on Election Day.\nNo previous experience or political knowled
 ge is required—just a willingness to serve your campus community and help
  others participate in our democracy. Our team will provide all the train
 ing\, resources\, and support you need to feel comfortable talking with f
 ellow students and answering common questions about voter registration an
 d upcoming elections.\nAs New Jersey's voter registration deadline approa
 ches\, volunteers will work alongside Civic and Voter Engagement staff to
  reach students across campus through pop-up voter registration stations 
 and outreach efforts. Together\, we'll help ensure every student has acce
 ss to accurate\, trusted\, and nonpartisan election information.\nAs a vo
 lunteer\, you will learn how to:\n\nAssist students with registering to v
 ote or updating their voter registration\nEncourage fellow students to pl
 edge to vote on Election Day\nAnswer common questions about voter registr
 ation and voting options\nConnect students with trusted\, nonpartisan ele
 ction resources\nEngage in respectful\, nonpartisan conversations about c
 ivic participation\nHelp create a campus culture that values democratic e
 ngagement\n\nBy participating\, you'll gain valuable leadership\, communi
 cation\, and outreach skills while making a meaningful impact on campus. 
 Every conversation has the potential to inspire someone to participate in
  our democracy\, and every new voter strengthens our community.\nWhether 
 you're passionate about civic engagement or simply looking for a meaningf
 ul way to give back on the 9/11 Day of Service\, this is an opportunity t
 o serve your fellow students while helping build a more informed\, engage
 d\, and connected campus.\nNo experience is necessary—just bring your ent
 husiasm\, a willingness to make a difference\, and a commitment to servin
 g others. Together\, we'll help every Red Hawk get election ready\, one c
 onversation at a time.\n \n******Please Note: You must register for this 
 event via the following link\, RSVPing here does not secure your spot****
 *\n\nHosted by: Civic & Voter Engagement\, Office of Community Engagement
  and Partnerships\n\nAdditional Information can be found at: https://mont
 clair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12539811
DTEND:20260912T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20260822T020556Z
DTSTART:20260912T130000Z
LOCATION:Student Center 419
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
