BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Montclair State University
CATEGORIES:ThoughtfulLearning
CATEGORIES:Service
CATEGORIES:Medium Size
CATEGORIES:Civics
DESCRIPTION:Join thousands of colleges\, universities\, nonprofits\, busin
 esses\, and community organizations across the country as we celebrate Na
 tional Voter Registration Day—the nation's largest single-day voter regis
 tration effort. This annual\, nonpartisan initiative brings Americans tog
 ether with one shared goal: helping eligible voters get registered\, info
 rmed\, and prepared to participate in our democracy.\nJoin us on Septembe
 r 17 from 12:00–4:00 PM in the Student Center Ballrooms and Quad as Montc
 lair State University celebrates this national movement with an afternoon
  of civic engagement\, entertainment\, and community.\nThis year's event 
 is proudly presented in collaboration with the Office of Commuter Life as
  part of Commuter Life Appreciation Week (CLAW). Together\, we're celebra
 ting the important role commuter students play in our campus community wh
 ile encouraging every Red Hawk to become an informed and engaged particip
 ant in our democracy.\nWhether you're registering to vote for the first t
 ime\, updating your voter registration\, or learning more about the upcom
 ing election\, Race to the Ballot is your one-stop destination to get ele
 ction ready.\nThe event will kick off with welcoming remarks from Montcla
 ir State University President Dr. Jonathan Koppell\, who will officially 
 open the celebration by speaking about the importance of civic participat
 ion and the power of student voices. Throughout the afternoon\, you'll al
 so hear from special guest speakers who will share their perspectives on 
 the importance of voting\, civic leadership\, and making a difference in 
 our communities.\nEnjoy a fun-filled afternoon featuring:\n\nA giant patr
 iotic inflatable obstacle course\nYard games and interactive activities\n
 Free food served throughout the event\nMusic\, giveaways\, and civic swag
 \nVoter registration assistance and nonpartisan election resources\nInter
 active activities hosted by campus and community partners\n\nBe sure to s
 tay for the entire event! Students who remain through the closing program
  will be entered into a raffle for a chance to win an exciting grand priz
 e.\nTogether\, we're joining a nationwide effort that has helped millions
  of Americans prepare to vote. Race to the Ballot is more than a voter re
 gistration event—it's a celebration of civic participation\, community\, 
 and the belief that every voice has the power to shape the future.\nThe r
 ace starts here. The finish line is the ballot box. Register\, get inform
 ed\, and join the movement!\n\nHosted by: Civic & Voter Engagement\, Camp
 us Activities at Bloomfield\, Office of Commuter Life\n\nAdditional Infor
 mation can be found at: https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/125
 39388
DTEND:20260916T180000Z
DTSTAMP:20260822T020556Z
DTSTART:20260916T160000Z
LOCATION:Deacon's Den and Talbott Hall Quad
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:(Bloomfield Campus) National Voter Registration Day: Race to the B
 allot
UID:https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12539388
URL:https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12539388
X-HOSTS:Office of Commuter Life
END:VEVENT
